summary: Verify that LTP timer tests exercise arm_arch_timer driver via ftrace
description: |
    This test compiles and runs two LTP timer-related test cases:
    - timer_create01
    - futex_wait05

    It sets up function-level ftrace tracing and verifies that the
    `arch_timer_handler_phys` and `arch_timer_set_next_event_phys` functions
    are invoked. These confirm that the arm_arch_timer driver is responsible
    for handling timer expiration and scheduling on the platform.

    The script:
      - Clones LTP sources
      - Builds only the specified tests (no full LTP install)
      - Configures ftrace
      - Runs each test and captures traces
      - Parses the trace log to confirm function invocation

    Expected result:
        [   PASS   ] :: timer_create01 executed
        [   PASS   ] :: arch_timer_handler_phys was called
        [   PASS   ] :: arch_timer_set_next_event_phys was called
        [   PASS   ] :: futex_wait05 executed
        [   PASS   ] :: arch_timer_handler_phys was called
        [   PASS   ] :: arch_timer_set_next_event_phys was called
        OVERALL RESULT: PASS
contact: Rakesh Musalay <rmusalay@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
duration: 10m
enabled: true
id: 2366cc3d-7621-4017-8980-981d3b3d5d14
